# RELEASE 15 BUG (a real one, in the 1981 game). The TIMBER ROOM,
# one move west of here, is a landmine: dropping any HELD item there
# -- or taking inventory -- drives the room-contents lister into
# infinite recursion. The routine at packed address 6626 calls
# itself forever and never advances to the next object; on period
# interpreters those nested frames blew the fixed stack and crashed
# the game, and the game's own platform contract caps total stack
# usage far below what this consumes (Z-Machine Standard 6.3.3).
# The object tree stays perfectly consistent throughout, so this is
# the game's logic, not data corruption.
#
# THE WORKAROUND, and surely how 1981 players survived: drop
# everything HERE at Ladder Bottom instead, and pass through the
# Timber Room empty-handed. Entering and leaving the room is safe;
# only inventory-touching actions inside it recurse.

drop all
w. w
get coal and candles and screwdriver

s
open lid
put coal in machine
close lid
turn switch with screwdriver
drop screwdriver
open lid
get diamond
n
put diamond in basket
drop candles

# A knock-on from the Timber Room workaround: in the v1/v3 routes
# the lit lamp was dropped IN the Timber Room and lit it for the
# return trip. Here the lamp lies one room further east at Ladder
# Bottom, so the Timber Room is pitch black on the way back. The
# squeeze refuses even the candles ("You cannot fit through this
# passage with that load"), so the answer is one empty-handed dash
# through the dark -- straight east, touching nothing (grue risk,
# and the drop-landmine besides). Under THIS seed the grue passes
# on the snack; if the SEED directive ever changes, re-verify this
# dash survives.

e
e
get all

